  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nMuch of the thunderstorm activity has been centered near the I-70\ncorridor. Additional thunderstorms have developed across Indiana and\nwill work into portions of the region a well. Additional storms have\ndeveloped south the region and have the potential to move into\nsouthern portions of the region. Not all locations will receive rain\nhowever with storms being scattered in nature. \n\nWhile widespread severe weather is not expected, isolated strong to\nsevere storms will still be possible. In addition, these storms will\nproduce heavy downpours and could lead to localized flooding issues.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nSunday into Monday, a weak mid-level disturbance will slowly shift \neast through our area with showers and storms possible each day. \nInstability will be much less as winds shift to the north behind a \nweak frontal boundary. This will limit the severe storm threat.",
